From: Eicke Hecht <eicke.hecht@outlook.de>
Subject: [PATCH] qemu-arm: whitelist the eicke A/B env variables

CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC is a board-header define (not Kconfig), so it
cannot be set from a .cfg fragment. Together with CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST
(set in eicke-env-fat.cfg) it restricts which variables may be modified at
runtime or imported from the attacker-writable uboot.env on the FAT boot
partition: the eicke A/B state contract (rootdev/ustate/bootcount, see
doc/images/eicke-update-image.md in meta-eicke) plus the variables the
eicke boot script assigns itself before use (bootargs/slot/fdt_addr_r).
Everything else keeps its compiled-in default.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [eicke product configuration]

--- a/include/configs/qemu-arm.h
+++ b/include/configs/qemu-arm.h
@@ -11,4 +11,11 @@

 /* For timer, QEMU emulates an ARMv7/ARMv8 architected timer */

+/* eicke: with CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST only these variables may be set at
+ * runtime / imported from uboot.env on the FAT boot partition: the A/B state
+ * contract (rootdev/ustate/bootcount) plus the variables the eicke boot
+ * script assigns itself before use (bootargs/slot/fdt_addr_r). */
+#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC \
+	"rootdev:sw,ustate:dw,bootcount:dw,bootargs:sw,slot:dw,fdt_addr_r:xw"
+
 #endif /* __CONFIG_H */
